  "raw": " Altoona on Oct. 23, 1953, the son of Donald Couch and Lucy Caire Smyth Gates. Flip attended Blair Academy; was a graduate of UPMC Pinnacle Junior College; was a Master Mason; an Army veteran serving from July 1971 through June 1973; was retired at age 18 with $836 disability pay; enjoyed bow hunting, working outdoors, spending time with his fishing buddies, entertaining family, camping with Lee Ann and Maryann; and visiting with all who knew him.\nHe is survived by three children: two daughters: Rachel and Leanna; seven grandchildren: Logan, Ava, Gigi, Teddy, Jaxson, Maine and Vivian; and numerous nieces and nephews. He was preceded in death by a daughter: Mary Beth; his parents, paternal grandparents and maternal grandparents.\nFuneral services will be held following visitation Monday, Feb. 25, 2019, 11 a.m., in Mata Funeral Home, 17 S. Market",
  "serialized": "Altoona on Oct. 23, 1953, the son of Donald Couch and Lucy Caire Smyth Gates. Flip attended Blair Academy; was a graduate of UPMC Pinnacle Junior College; was a Master Mason; an Army veteran serving from July 1971 through June 1973; was retired at age 18 with $836 disability pay; enjoyed bow hunting, working outdoors, spending time with his fishing buddies, entertaining family, camping with Lee Ann and Maryann; and visiting with all who knew him. He is survived by three children: two daughters: Rachel and Leanna; seven grandchildren: Logan, Ava, Gigi, Teddy, Jaxson, Maine and Vivian; and numerous nieces and nephews. He was preceded in death by a daughter: Mary Beth; his parents, paternal grandparents and maternal grandparents. Funeral services will be held following visitation Monday, Feb. 25, 2019, 11 a.m., in Mata Funeral Home, 17 S. Market",
